In article <9001151935.AA27994@cie.uoregon.edu> ghudson@CIE.UOREGON.EDU writes:
>
>     Which brings us back to the question of what *is* the purpose of
>polymorphing items?
>
Why not place a limit on the size of the pile on a particular location?
Is reasonable now to have 30 armor pieces, 30 weapons, 300 rocks, plus
various other items piled on one spot?  Such a pile would reach the ceiling!
And it certainly would be difficult to just waltz over it.  In "reality,"
things added to a big pile would slide down into adjacent spaces.  And if the
pile were big enough you couldn't walk on it unless you kicked stuff off the
pile first.  (Hmmm, you could climb the pile though, attack from the top, or
climb through a hole in the ceiling (that you just dug), or rain rocks down
on monsters nearby, or ...).  Anyway, this could alleviate (or at least
lessen) the complaints that polymorphing huge piles makes the game too easy:
the piles would be smaller.

